From 5d344efea99a9339dd51c78c5ee677e66f217e97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Suno <engineering@projectSuno.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:58:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] app-info: Identify Suno applications

Applications Suno installs from package files run in the
Suno_application.process SELinux domain under a category pair allocated
to them, in their own app-Suno-NAME-PID.scope. Name them through Suno's
resolver (org.projectSuno.AppPermissions1.Identify, the rules Mutter 0041
uses) and treat them as sandboxed: permissions are stored under their ID
and files they are given go through the document portal. One that cannot
be named is refused instead of being treated as the host. Identify is
asked only of the name's verified owner: the root-owned
/usr/libexec/Suno-app-permissions in Suno-app-permissions.service, in the
portal's own mount namespace.
